      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-26T02:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>K.N.Y.F.E.'s powers come from her tech, not mutant powers. Not sure that F.I.L.T.E.R. would employ someone not 'pure' human.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sort of. &nbsp;From her bio:</p>\n<blockquote>\n However, spending over a decade around the The Block’s occupants and its temporal containment systems irrevocably altered her physiology, which took more of a toll on Huntly than it did most. &nbsp;  She spent weeks in the neo-superhuman development wing of the infirmary as energy spikes erupted all over her body. \n</blockquote>\n So, she's not a mutant in that she wasn't born that way, but her powers definitely go beyond just her tech. &nbsp;And they definitely did keep her on the payroll after she was \"mutated\".",
