    {
      "id": 110250,
      "name": "Medic-Tank",
      "username": "Medic-Tank",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-26T19:11:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Under3\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/under3/48/1872_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Under3:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I took it as those spikes of energy come from an attack from Dawn and aren't K.N.Y.F.E.'s.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>One of them has the same shape and placement as on the card For the Greater Good and we've seen dawn attack with energy blasts but not spikes that remain as far as I know. Most of the spikes have one end hidden but the few we see completely are sharp on both edges which is more consistent with an internal origin than having the control to precisely get them all planted halfway. Of course it all brings the question on how energy spikes deal with her suit. Her incap also seems reminescent from her origin and I quote from her bio:&nbsp;''She spent weeks in the neo-superhuman development wing of the infirmary as energy spikes erupted all over her body.''</p>\n<p>In fact it just struck me how strange it is for a dimensional prison to even have a neo-superhuman development wing…</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:41:12.587Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
